<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply rises to 16.3 pct on May 9.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply rises to 16.3 pct on May 9.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.3 percent on May 9, up from 16.1 percent on April 25, 1997, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   May 9, 1997    Apr 25, 1997  May 10, 1996</p>
<p>		   16.3	     16.1	    15.9</p>
<p>Money supply was 7,181.39 billion rupees on May 9, 1997, against 7,111.78 billion on April 25, 1997 and compared to 6,174.76 billion rupees on May 10, 1996, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
